        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your patient, a 74-year-old male, admitted on 24/12/2006 due to an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD). On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Clinical examination, chest X-ray, arterial blood gas analysis, and pulse oximetry confirmed the exacerbation. Blood tests were obtained to exclude infection and assess general status. The patient was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and received appropriate patient education regarding his condition and inhaler technique. He responded well to treatment with improvement of symptoms and oxygen saturation. He was discharged on 25/12/2006 in stable condition. Please arrange follow-up and consider pulmonary rehabilitation. Discharge medications and further recommendations are enclosed.</div>"
            },
